# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# The configuration level of the bench guards (docs/rt1060-management-image-feasibility.md). A test form cannot
# take effect unless the declaration holds, and the declaration holds only on this board with the TRNG and no
# test entropy. Zephyr reports an assignment that Kconfig drops, because a dependency is not met, as a WARNING
# and goes on (the finding of docs/ssh-integrated-image.md). The CMake level turns it into a refusal: it
# requires CONFIG_CRUX_MANAGEMENT_BENCH_IMAGE and every selected form to be set.

config CRUX_MANAGEMENT_BENCH_IMAGE
	bool "Declared RT1060-EVKB rev B bench image of the integrated management composition"
	depends on BOARD_MIMXRT1060_EVK_MIMXRT1062_QSPI && BOARD_REVISION = "B"
	depends on ENTROPY_MCUX_TRNG && !TEST_RANDOM_GENERATOR && !FAKE_ENTROPY_NATIVE_SIM
	depends on !NET_DHCPV4 && !NET_IPV6
	depends on !WOLFSSL_RSA
	depends on !WOLFSSL_HAS_SETTINGS_FILE
	depends on NET_TCP_ISN_RFC6528
	help
	  The declaration that allows the test forms below, for this board and this bench only. It is the
	  Kconfig level of three: the CMake level is bench_guard.cmake and the C level is src/bench_guard.h.
	  It needs the TRNG driver and no test entropy, and no DHCP and no IPv6, because the listeners
	  answer on the one bench address (D10). It needs wolfCrypt built without RSA (D11, row C9): the declared
	  profile uses none, and a wolfSSL settings file would hide whether RSA is built. It needs the RFC 6528 initial
	  sequence number (D-c, row C11), which the build-local Zephyr copy's second patch makes fail closed: without it
	  Zephyr takes the number from sys_rand32_get() and the patch protects nothing.

if CRUX_MANAGEMENT_BENCH_IMAGE

# A test form is a way of doing something that is acceptable on a bench and is not acceptable as a
# product. Each one depends on the declaration. A symbol added here must start with CRUX_BENCH_, so that
# check_bench_guard.py finds it, and must be listed in bench_declaration.json.

config CRUX_BENCH_TEST_HOST_KEY
	bool "SSH host key in test form: a static buffer, never wiped (D5)"
	help
	  The credential store generates the key from the TRNG and the provider borrows it from a static
	  buffer for the life of the image. No product rule exists for holding and wiping a host key.

config CRUX_BENCH_NO_TIME_SOURCE
	bool "No time source: times are relative to boot (D7)"
	depends on !RTC
	help
	  Zephyr's realtime clock, which nothing sets. Certificates and events carry boot-relative times.

config CRUX_BENCH_FILE_RAM_DISK
	bool "RAM disk as the file backend (D2)"
	depends on DISK_DRIVER_RAM && !DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC
	help
	  The file service, the credential store and the events' files live on a RAM disk in SDRAM. Nothing
	  persists across a reset, and no card is touched: the SD card driver is not in the image. The
	  composition formats the RAM disk when it mounts blank, and never formats anything else
	  (src/bench_medium.c).

config CRUX_BENCH_FILE_MICROSD
	bool "microSD card as the file backend (D2). Reserved for a later run: not selected in this image"
	depends on DISK_DRIVER_SDMMC && !DISK_DRIVER_RAM
	help
	  The existing microSD provider. A later run selects it by changing the state of this form in
	  bench_declaration.json to selected, with the owner's approval of a card run and the M4 microSD
	  tools. Even then a mount that fails is reported and the card is never formatted by this image.

config CRUX_BENCH_FIRST_ACCOUNT_FILE
	bool "First account from a password in a file outside the repository (D3)"
	help
	  The password is read at configuration from the file that CRUX_BENCH_PASSWORD_FILE names, which must be private,
	  outside every git work tree and at least 16 characters, and is embedded in this image as plaintext in read-only
	  data, because Access takes a plaintext password and derives its own record. The build records the file's
	  SHA-256 in the manifest and never the password. A product creates its first account in a serial setup step.

endif # CRUX_MANAGEMENT_BENCH_IMAGE
